  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to finance through lending</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A community-based, trust-driven mechanism for accessing finance without formal banking (in Ethiopia called eQUB).The main objective is to help households and SMEs switch to cleaner cooking solutions, improve health and environmental outcomes, and create a simple, affordable, and scalable way for communities to access these technologies.The eQUB is structured around three core pillars:1. User Empowerment through familiar tools of financial inclusion.2. Community-driven adoption of clean cooking.3. Sustainable infrastructure and long-term scalability.</narrative>
  </description>
